+A server can cap reasoning **server-side**, and `quality-test.sh` reads that budget back — it sends nothing for
+it. Both spellings are read, because the engines spell it differently:
+
+* **vLLM / SGLang** (the qwen3.8 and ThinkingCap composes, from their effort-budget PRs): a budget chosen by the
+  request's effort (`scripts/lib/effort_budget.py`; `THINKING_BUDGETS=off` turns it off). Its entrypoint prints
+  one `[effort-budget] v1 …` line at boot, which is what gets read — from `docker logs`, the **last** line, since
+  the log spans restarts — for the run's `REASONING_EFFORT` or the server's default effort.
+* **llama.cpp**: the `--reasoning-budget N` **boot flag**, and no boot line to read. The shipped composes emit it
+  as `${REASONING_BUDGET:-32768}` (32768 has been the qwen3.8 llama.cpp default since
+  [#1617](https://github.com/noonghunna/club-3090/issues/1617)), so a *present* flag proves nothing: the wrapper
+  resolves its **value** through the container env exactly as `--thinking-budget` verifies it
+  (`scripts/lib/thinking-budget.sh`), falling back to a compose's own `[reasoning] budget=N` boot line when the
+  container's argv is not visible (a remote `llama-server`). There is no effort map, so the stamp carries no
+  `(effort E)` part.
+
+A budget applies to every request the server serves — the in-sandbox agentic packs' own calls included:
 
